# text_id = 1559
# text = Most untypically for the House of Commons , and even more untypically for a Conservative Government , we are abolishing the tried , if imperfect , system that we know and substituting an untried system that has obvious flaws , and little to commend it that is new or relevant to the 1980s in which it will begin operation .
