# text_id = 1667
# text = If there was ever a time when we should emphasise again and again the need for a fundamental reform of the procedures of the House of Commons so that it can be an effective brake and an effective scrutineer of the conduct of the Executive , especially on and of the borrowing money from abroad , this is that time .
