# text_id = 1698
# text = According to Mr. Josling , the cost of the switch from deficiency payments to the Common Market farm policy would amount , in the case of an old age pensioner couple , to between 50 p and £ 1 a week — and those figures will not be found in the pamphlets which the Government published last summer , at public expense , about the effects of joining the Common Market .
