# text = The principal Act was remiss , in that somebody under 16 years of age could be left in sole charge and a customer might come along ; and the person under 16 might be incapable of deciding whether the customer was sufficiently experienced to take a horse out on his own , or , if he was not experienced , what sort of pony or horse he should have .
