# text_id = 1752
# text = Because of the close - knit nature of the aluminium industry in Britain — and I will not use any other description — many users of aluminium , both manufactured and semi- fabricated , are paying and will continue to pay vastly above world price for aluminium that those subsidised smelters produce , and they regard that as entirely wrong , for it makes no kind of sense economically .
