# text_id = 1765
# text = We are living in a complex scientific world — a world becoming more complex every day — in which life is becoming scientifically based , in which politicians and lawyers have very little knowledge of some of the influences and developments at work , yet one in which responsibility for the administration of the changes and problems brought about by science falls directly upon the legislative assemblies of the nations .
