# text_id = 1781
# text = High private rents for furnished accommodation could be justified if private landlords and those renting out private accommodation were investing the capital that they receive by way of rents into putting up more property for renting at reasonable prices , but we know that the tremendous rise in land prices in the last couple of years has virtually made that prospect one that is just a mirage on the horizon .
