# text_id = 1793
# text = The Secretary of State , when this matter was raised in another place , said that he regarded it as one of some significance ; that he was aware of the arguments both ways ; but that he did not think it right in a Bill dealing entirely with electoral machinery to try to make any change concerning the proscription of an organisation which may have been banned for other reasons .
