# text_id = 1841
# text = The Land Commission Act was only necessary because Mr. Harold Macmillan , when he was the Minister of Housing and Local Government , chopped all the financial provisions of the 1947 Act , which was introduced by my noble friend Lord Silkin and has been the cornerstone of all post - war planning , without any real regard for the effect that that would have on the other sections .
