# text_id = 1876
# text = Therefore , it is natural that we should try to preserve the pattern of shipbuilding , and it was perhaps reached in its most developed sense by my hon . Friend the Member for Belfast , East ( Mr. McMaster ) , who not only knew roughly where ships ought to be made , but said that it was better for this country to concentrate upon the specialised type of ship .
