# text = That will be the main decision before the Scottish people , and it will be perfectly rational for each elector to vote on the basis of which party he believes will screw most money out of Westminster , because he knows that the taxation consequences for him will be relatively small , since he will pay only one - ninth of the additional taxation flowing from that additional public expenditure .
